@startuml GupShup Cafe - Communication Diagram (Socket Events)

' PlantUML version 1.2025.x
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

title GupShup Cafe - Socket.io Event Communication (Testing Branch)

' Actors
actor "Client\n(React App)" as Client
participant "Socket.io\nClient" as SocketClient
participant "Socket.io\nServer" as SocketServer
participant "Socket\nHandlers" as Handlers
participant "Room\nManager" as RoomMgr
participant "Agent\nService" as AgentSvc
database "Database" as DB

== Connection & Authentication ==

Client -> SocketClient: Initialize socket
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **connect**\n{auth: {userId, campusOrLocation}}
SocketServer -> Handlers: on_connect(sid, auth)
Handlers --> SocketClient: **connection-ack**\n{socketId, connected: true}

== Room Discovery & Join ==

Client -> SocketClient: Join room
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **join-room**\n{roomId, userData, metadata}
SocketServer -> Handlers: on_join_room(sid, data)
Handlers -> RoomMgr: join_room(roomId, participant)
RoomMgr -> DB: save participant
Handlers --> SocketServer: Broadcast to room
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **participants-update**\n{participants[]}
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **participant-joined**\n{participant}
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **room-update**\n{roomState}

== Room Lobby - Ready Check ==

Client -> SocketClient: Mark ready
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **user-ready**\n{isReady: true}
SocketServer -> Handlers: on_user_ready(sid, data)
Handlers -> RoomMgr: set_participant_ready(sid, true)
Handlers --> SocketServer: Broadcast to room
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **participants-update**\n{participants[]}

note right
  When all participants ready
  and minimum met:
  auto-start discussion
end note

== Discussion Start ==

Handlers -> RoomMgr: check_and_start_discussion()
RoomMgr -> DB: update room status
RoomMgr -> AgentSvc: create_facilitator_agent()
Handlers --> SocketServer: Broadcast to room
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **discussion-started**\n{room, currentSpeaker, round: 1}
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **turn-started**\n{speaker, timeRemaining}

== WebRTC Audio Connection Setup ==

Client -> SocketClient: Request WebRTC setup
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **ready-for-webrtc**\n{participantId}
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **webrtc-setup-ready**\n{participants[]}

Client -> SocketClient: Create offer
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **webrtc-offer**\n{to: peerId, sdp: offer}
SocketServer -> Handlers: on_webrtc_offer(sid, data)
Handlers --> SocketServer: Send to specific peer
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **webrtc-offer**\n{from: peerId, sdp: offer}

Client -> SocketClient: Create answer
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **webrtc-answer**\n{to: peerId, sdp: answer}
SocketServer -> Handlers: on_webrtc_answer(sid, data)
Handlers --> SocketServer: Send to specific peer
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **webrtc-answer**\n{from: peerId, sdp: answer}

Client -> SocketClient: ICE candidates
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **webrtc-ice-candidate**\n{to: peerId, candidate}
SocketServer -> Handlers: on_webrtc_ice_candidate(sid, data)
Handlers --> SocketServer: Send to specific peer
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **webrtc-ice-candidate**\n{from: peerId, candidate}

note right
  WebRTC connection states:
  - connection-created
  - connection-verified
  - connection-failed
  - connection-restored
  - connection-closed
  - peer-disconnected
end note

== Audio State Management ==

Client -> SocketClient: Mute/unmute
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **audio-state-change**\n{isMuted, participantId}
SocketServer -> Handlers: Update participant state
Handlers --> SocketServer: Broadcast to room
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **participants-update**\n{participants[]}

Client -> SocketClient: Audio level
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **audio-level-update**\n{level, participantId}
SocketServer --> SocketClient: (no response - passive monitoring)

== Speech Transcription ==

Client -> SocketClient: Transcript ready
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **transcript-received**\n{participantId, roomId, text,\nconfidence, timestamp}
SocketServer -> Handlers: on_transcript_received(sid, data)
Handlers -> DB: save transcript
Handlers -> AgentSvc: process_transcript_for_feedback()\n(background task)
Handlers --> SocketServer: Broadcast to room
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **transcript-update**\n{participantId, text}

note right
  Background processing:
  - EnglishFeedbackAgent
  - Grammar analysis via MCP
  - Instant feedback (2-3 sec)
end note

== English Feedback (AI Agent) ==

Client -> SocketClient: Request instant feedback
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **get-instant-feedback**\n{participantId}
SocketServer -> Handlers: on_get_instant_feedback(sid, data)
Handlers -> AgentSvc: get_instant_feedback(participantId)
AgentSvc --> Handlers: feedback data
Handlers --> SocketServer: Send to specific user
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **english-feedback**\n{feedback: {grammar, vocabulary,\nfluency, suggestions}}

note right
  Feedback is private
  to the participant
end note

== AI Facilitator Turn ==

RoomMgr -> Handlers: Next speaker is facilitator
Handlers --> SocketServer: Broadcast to room
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **speaker-change**\n{speaker: facilitatorAgent,\nisFacilitator: true}

Client -> SocketClient: Request facilitator response
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **request-facilitator-response**\n{roomId}
SocketServer -> Handlers: on_request_facilitator_response()
Handlers -> AgentSvc: generate_facilitator_response(context)
AgentSvc --> Handlers: response text
Handlers --> SocketServer: Broadcast to room
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **facilitator-response**\n{text, speaker: facilitatorAgent}

note right
  AI facilitator:
  - Guides discussion
  - Asks follow-up questions
  - Maintains flow
  - Generated via Strands SDK
end note

== Turn Management ==

note over RoomMgr
  Timer running on backend
  60 seconds per turn (default)
end note

Handlers --> SocketServer: Timer warning
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **timer-warning**\n{timeRemaining: 10}

Handlers --> SocketServer: Turn ended
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **turn-ended**\n{speaker}

RoomMgr -> RoomMgr: advance_to_next_speaker()
Handlers --> SocketServer: Next turn started
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **turn-started**\n{speaker, timeRemaining}
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **speaker-change**\n{newSpeaker, previousSpeaker}

== Round Completion ==

RoomMgr -> RoomMgr: check_round_completion()
Handlers --> SocketServer: Round complete
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **round-complete**\n{round: 1, totalRounds: 3}
Handlers --> SocketServer: Next round starts
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **turn-started**\n{speaker, round: 2}

== Discussion End ==

RoomMgr -> RoomMgr: check_discussion_completion()
RoomMgr -> DB: update room status = COMPLETED
RoomMgr -> AgentSvc: generate_comprehensive_feedback()
Handlers --> SocketServer: Broadcast to room
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **discussion-ended**\n{room, summary, feedback}
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **comprehensive-feedback**\n{feedback per participant}

== Disconnect & Cleanup ==

Client -> SocketClient: Leave room
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **leave-room**
SocketServer -> Handlers: on_leave_room(sid)
Handlers -> RoomMgr: remove_participant(sid)
RoomMgr -> DB: update participant left_at
Handlers --> SocketServer: Broadcast to room
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **participant-left**\n{participantId}
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **participants-update**\n{participants[]}

Client -> SocketClient: Disconnect
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **disconnect**
SocketServer -> Handlers: on_disconnect(sid)
Handlers -> RoomMgr: cleanup_participant(sid)

note right
  Graceful cleanup:
  - Close peer connections
  - Stop timers
  - Save final state
  - Remove from room
end note

== Broadcast Test Events (Development) ==

Client -> SocketClient: Join broadcast test
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **join-broadcast-test**\n{role: speaker/listener}
SocketServer -> Handlers: Setup test environment
Handlers --> SocketServer: Broadcast
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **broadcast-test-role**\n{role}
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **broadcast-test-participants**\n{participants[]}

Client -> SocketClient: Reset broadcast test
SocketClient -> SocketServer: **reset-broadcast-test**
Handlers --> SocketServer: Broadcast
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **broadcast-test-reset**

note right
  Development-only events
  for testing WebRTC
  with multiple participants
end note

== Error Handling ==

SocketServer --> SocketClient: **connect_error**\n{message, code}
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **error**\n{message, type}
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **room-error**\n{message, roomId}
SocketServer --> SocketClient: **webrtc-error**\n{message, peerId}

note as EventSummary
**Socket Event Categories:**

**Connection (3):**
- connect, disconnect, connect_error

**Room Management (7):**
- join-room, leave-room, room-update
- participant-joined, participant-left
- participants-update, role-change

**Discussion Flow (7):**
- discussion-started, discussion-ended
- turn-started, turn-ended
- speaker-change, next-speaker
- round-complete

**WebRTC Signaling (15):**
- ready-for-webrtc, webrtc-setup-ready
- webrtc-offer, webrtc-answer
- webrtc-ice-candidate
- webrtc-connection-* (10 states)

**Audio State (3):**
- audio-state-change
- audio-level-update
- microphone-permission-change

**AI & Feedback (4):**
- transcript-received, transcript-update
- english-feedback, get-instant-feedback
- request-facilitator-response
- facilitator-response
- comprehensive-feedback

**Timer (2):**
- timer-warning, timer-expired

**Broadcast Test (4):**
- join-broadcast-test
- broadcast-test-role
- broadcast-test-participants
- broadcast-test-reset

**Total: 45+ events**
end note

@enduml
